WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.720 line:87%
This Luthier was asked
what makes a good guitar

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.960 line:94%
and the answer was a good person.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.960 line:94%
And I really liked that. I think it's...

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.400 line:87%
The personality of the maker
comes through in the instrument.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.640 line:87%
The Leonardo Guitar Research Project
is a three-year project

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.000 line:87%
to investigate the use
of non-tropical woods in guitar-making.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.480 line:94%
Tropical woods are very common

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.880 line:87%
and are almost seen as necessary
for guitar-making.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.240 line:87%
And what we're trying to show
is that that may not be the case -

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.080 line:87%
that we can build perfectly good guitars
with non-tropical woods.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.480 line:87%
There are three schools
involved in the project.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.080 line:87%
There's Newark School in England,
there's CMB in Belgium

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.960 line:94%
and IKATA in Finland.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.800 line:94%
So far, we've had two workshops.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.080 line:87%
There's been great interaction between
the students from the different schools.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.760 line:87%
They're getting on very well
and exchanging a lot of ideas.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.520 line:87%
For the purpose
of this week's workshop,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.480 line:87%
we've samples of several species
of non-tropical wood

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.720 line:87%
and we're testing the workability
of the woods -

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.920 line:87%
how easy they are
to plane, saw, drill, fret, bend.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.560 line:87%
We're testing their flexibility
and also sound transmission.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.640 line:87%
We have four entrepreneurial Luthiers
involved in the project

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.440 line:87%
and their role is
to host a kind of apprenticeship

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.000 line:94%
just for a week or two.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.720 line:94%
So, the craft skills are important,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.360 line:87%
but equally important
is the business side of things,

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.920 line:87%
which enables the Luthier
to make a living.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.440 line:94%
The school is a place of education

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.760 line:87%
and the broader that education can be,
the more useful it is.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:55.880 line:87%
What the Erasmus+ project
enables us to do

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:58.840 line:87%
is collaborate in a way
that we all learn from each other.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.040 line:94%
It expands the horizons of each school

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.680 line:87%
and I think it helps the students
to feel like part of community.

